cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Explicit disorder thresholds for the coarse-graining cascade of the log-correlated model, formalized in Lean 4"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/GMCExplicitDelta"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of explicit disorder
  thresholds for the cutoff-uniform coarse-graining cascade of the
  log-correlated (Gaussian multiplicative chaos) model of a Brownian particle
  in a log-correlated potential. For d = 2, 3, 4 and every model whose
  disorder strength satisfies delta <= 0.36665, 0.18870, 0.15698
  respectively, the normalized defect of the cutoff coefficient on every cube
  above the cutoff scale is bounded in L^32 by an explicit constant times
  delta^2, and the expected directional energy by another explicit constant
  times delta^2, uniformly in the cutoff. The model and its vocabulary are
  those of the public subdiffusive-process formalization. The library contains
  no sorry and no custom axiom.
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
  - family-names: Kuusi
    given-names: Tuomo
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - homogenization
  - renormalization
  - Gaussian multiplicative chaos
license: Apache-2.0
